00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.670 align:start position:0%
 
we are overdue  for our continuation of the x-men film  franchise and that brings us to x-men  first class  now normally i'm not big on prequels  they've got a lot of inherent issues one  of them being we know where these  characters are going to end up later so  it takes a lot of the stakes out despite  my reservations this actually turned out  really well and was a really important  step for the franchise in a lot of ways  the first being the omission of  wolverine it was really important that  there finally be a film that establishes  x-men as a franchise does not begin and  end with wolverine because he'd been the  focus of every single film let's get the  focus back on professor x and magneto as  i pointed out when i talked about the  first x-men film there are a lot more  continuity issues with this than i had  initially thought when watching the  continuity errors are not the fault of  this film and actually i gotta say they  they ultimately made the right call to  accept certain continuity errors  for the sake of telling a better story  things like where professor xavier said  that he met a magneto as a teenager and  obviously we're seeing them meet for the  first time in their 30s so there's those  sorts of decisions being made set  continuity errors aside this is a really  tight film and there's not too much to  complain about here they make really  good use of the period setting that sort  of  james bond they're a spy feel that you  kind of get to it that's a really good  thing to pull from it and they avoid all  the 60s cliches of hippies and counter  culture and all that other junk that's  just been done to death  casting  really nicely done because given that  they already had iconic performances  given by patrick stewart and ian  mckellen you need to get really good  actors  actors who are good enough to pick  pieces that will evoke what the other  actors have done so that you can see the  connection but are also confident enough  in themselves to do their own thing so  it's not an impression at any point they  can be younger they can be brashered  they can they can have things different  about the characters because we know  they're gonna go through a lot of  personal changes in a journey i think it  was also a good call not to have too  many recurring characters ones we'd  already seen basically all we've got  we've got professor x and magneto we've  got mystique  that's pretty much it as far as direct  um characters that we've seen before oh  no there is one more um and that's beast  and choosing to have hank mccoy front  and center actually a pretty good call  especially considering we're not gonna  see him go through a physical  transformation until a little after the  halfway mark so he was a good call to  bring back as well pretty much everybody  else though  is all fresh blood which is a really  good idea by filling out the rest of the  x-men team with characters we have not  seen before havoc angel darwin banshee  this gives us the opportunity to throw  in characters where you don't know if  they're gonna make it because we haven't  seen them later on they could very well  die  unfortunately most of these filler  characters feel like just that they feel  like filler characters i'm not sure  there was much that could be done about  that though because the focus really  needs to be so strongly on professor x  and magneto that they were always just  gonna be side characters the action  there's a decent amount of action in  this film but it doesn't feel like an  action film it feels much more  intellectual which is a bit more in line  with x2 so it's nice to be getting that  feeling back as well  um matthew vaughn who came on to direct  this it almost feels like in a way he's  kind of apologizing for x-men the last  stand he's saying look because i left  that film i couldn't guide it into  something better you got stuck with what  you had so here let me apologize and  give you what i hoped i could have given  you if i'd done the last stand effects  are all very good and it's much more  careful use of special effects than we  saw in x-men origins wolverine or in  x-men the last stand it's just a return  to form for the franchise i still  personally like x2 a little bit better  but i think this does give it a run for  its money and anyone who says that first  class is their favorite in the series i  i would not begrudge them that and now  we're going to be getting our sequel  basically to both this and x-men the  last stand in the form of days of future  past it's gonna be really interesting to  see how they pull this off so until next  time this council is adjourned

